{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/839044-ferals-comic-book-as-inspiration","id":839044,"title":"\"Ferals\" comic book as inspiration?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-29T03:37:05-08:00","id":839044,"title":"\"Ferals\" comic book as inspiration?","content":"Not so long ago I found this comic book by Avatar Press and I liked it. It's dark, dirty and extremely violent story, though it;s still have some solid plot line, good action and well-rounded characters (as for me at least). But can it be used as source of inspiration for WtF-games?<br /> Contra:<br /> -there is no spirit/shamanic atmosphere <br /> -the Ferals themselves are hardly werewolves (despite obvious similarity)<br /> -the story as is more about human nature (the bad side of it) than about supernatural world<br /> Pro;<br /> -they are <i>still</i> pretty much werewolves<br /> -the town of the Ferals is similar to Fire Touched village, which were described in one of the 1st edition's splat (an extremely conservative, Christian sect)<br /> -the Ferals have some... *cough*... really good style. Only after reading I found out for self, what exactly 2nd EDITION werewolf can do with human.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.laptopzombie.co.uk/media/Legacy/ferals.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.laptopzombie.co.uk/media/Legacy/ferals.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.laptopzombie.co.uk/media/Legacy/ferals.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.laptopzombie.co.uk/media/Legacy/ferals.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://50shadesofbloodandviscera.files.wordpress.com/2012/09/ferals8gore-662x1024.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://50shadesofbloodandviscera.files.wordpress.com/2012/09/ferals8gore-662x1024.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://50shadesofbloodandviscera.files.wordpress.com/2012/09/ferals8gore-662x1024.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://50shadesofbloodandviscera.files.wordpress.com/2012/09/ferals8gore-662x1024.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/ferals01gore.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pu...rals01gore.jpg</a><br /> <br /> So, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:32:17-08:00","id":839116,"title":"","content":"I certainly use it for inspiration for Wolf-Blooded, at the very least. The Ferals seem a bit like one with the Anger Issues Tell, but the going Dalu seems more progressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T11:50:02-08:00","id":839336,"title":"","content":"One of the options in the Chronicler's Guide for Werewolf had something that might fit it better.<br /> <br /> While I agree that the mindset of the communities is a good inspiration for wolf-blooded communities, if I was going to incorporate the ferals into the game I'd go a different way.<br /> <br /> One thing is have the women be represented by some sort of Advanced Tell. Something descended through their bloodline that allows them to basically turn people into wolf-blooded.<br /> <br /> The turning feral aspect I'd bring about as part of a rite, one that can be performed solely by wolf-blooded if necessary. It would require the sacrifice of one of their number, or a prisoner similar to Chesnutt was, and upon the culmination of the rite and the drinking of blood, they would become a werewolf. Not a true one, but basically a mix of the zi'ir from first edition and Vampire's revenants. Primal Urge 1, may not increase, stuck in gauru form and constantly in wasu-im, verging on basu-im, with easy triggers, including the horn. A lack of personal identity, as one is just lost to the Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> While I know the books reference Fenris a lot, as much as I liked the brutal attitude of the werewolves in it, I feel that because of it, in Forsaken it would be linked to Huzuruth-Ur, the Dire Wolf. Perhaps he tried to create a new Uratha, seeing himself as the true inheritor of Father Wolf's mantle, and the only result was the bloodline of women. You could tie in Rabid Wolf for the infectious disease and madness angle, or Fenris the Destroyer Wolf for their chaotic and destructive nature. But I think Dire Wolf would be a good source, providing you went with a Firstborn at 